The network includes the Extended APN-AMBR IE under the following two conditions (per Clauses 8.3.18.14 and 8.3.17.5 — though only 8.3.18.14 is provided, and it aligns with 8.3.6.17):

1. **The network wishes to transmit APN-AMBR values to the UE for possible uplink policy enforcement** (Cl. 8.3.18.14 and Cl. 8.3.6.17);  
2. **At least one of the APN-AMBR values to be transmitted exceeds the maximum value specified in the (basic) APN aggregate maximum bit rate information element (i.e., the 3-octet APN-AMBR IE defined in Cl. 9.9.4.2)** (Cl. 8.3.18.14 and Cl. 8.3.6.17).

Clauses 9.9.3.8 (DRX parameter) and 9.9.3.46 (Extended DRX parameters) — both explicitly refer to 3GPP TS 24.008:  
- Clause 9.9.3.8 refers to clause 10.5.5.6 in TS 24.008;  
- Clause 9.9.3.46 refers to clause 10.5.5.32 in TS 24.008.

Per Clause 4.2A, a UE configured for NAS signalling low priority **shall** set the low priority indicator to *"MS is not configured for NAS signalling low priority"* in the following cases:

- The UE is performing an **attach for emergency bearer services**;  
- The UE has a **PDN connection for emergency bearer services established** and is performing **EPS mobility management procedures**, or is **establishing a PDN connection for emergency bearer services**;  
- The UE is **configured for dual priority** and is **requested by upper layers** to establish a PDN connection with the low priority indicator set to *"MS is not configured for NAS signalling low priority"*;  
- The UE is **configured for dual priority** and is performing **EPS session management procedures** related to a PDN connection established with the low priority indicator set to *"MS is not configured for NAS signalling low priority"*;  
- The UE is **configured for dual priority**, has a PDN connection established with the low priority indicator set to *"MS is not configured for NAS signalling low priority"*, and is performing **EPS mobility management procedures**;  
- The UE is performing a **service request procedure for a CS fallback emergency call or 1xCS fallback emergency call**;  
- The UE is **configured to use AC11/15 in the selected PLMN**;  
- The UE is **responding to paging**.

The **SMS services status** IE is included in a **normal tracking area updating procedure for EPS services and "SMS only"** that was **successful for EPS services only** (i.e., EPS services accepted, SMS services not accepted), as specified in **Clause 8.2.26.19**.

Its inclusion signifies that:
- The tracking area update succeeded for EPS services (EPS update result = “EPS only”);
- The network **did not accept SMS services**, and the IE conveys the specific reason (e.g., “SMS services not available”, “SMS services not available in this PLMN”, or other values);
- This triggers UE-specific handling per **Clause 5.5.3.2.4A**, including actions on timers (T3430, T3411, T3402), the tracking area updating attempt counter, EPS update status, and service availability state.

It is **not included** if SMS services are fully accepted (in which case “SMS only” would appear in the *Additional update result* IE per Clause 8.2.26.14 and Clause 5.5.3.3.4.2).

Per Clause 5.5.1.2.2 and Clause 8.2.6.16, the UE **must** include the EPS NAS message container IE in the REGISTRATION REQUEST message during initial registration **if and only if** all of the following conditions are met:

1.  The UE was previously registered in S1 mode before entering state EMM-DEREGISTERED (Clause 5.5.1.2.2, item "i)" under "During initial registration the UE handles the 5GS mobile identity IE..." and Clause 8.2.6.16);
2.  The UE has received an "interworking without N26 interface not supported" indication from the network (Clause 5.5.1.2.2, item "ii)" and Clause 8.2.6.16);
3.  An EPS security context and a valid native 4G-GUTI are available (Clause 5.5.1.2.2, item "2)" and Clause 8.2.6.16).

The content of this IE is the complete integrity-protected ATTACH REQUEST message, using the EPS security context (Clause 8.2.6.16).

Upon receiving an RRCReject message, the UE shall perform the actions specified in Clause 5.3.15 (as referenced from Clauses 5.3.3.5 and 5.3.13.10), which are:

- Stop timers T300, T319, T319a, and T302 (if running);  
- Reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;  
- If *waitTime* is present in RRCReject: start T302 with that value;  
- If RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform upper layers that access barring applies for all access categories except '0' and '2';  
- If received in response to RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers of RRC connection setup failure (procedure ends);  
- If received in response to RRCResumeRequest or RRCResumeRequest1:  
  - If resume triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers of resume failure;  
  - If triggered by RNA update, or for SDT while T380 is not running: set *pendingRNA-Update* to true;  
  - Discard current K<sub>gNB</sub>, K<sub>UPenc</sub>, K<sub>UPint</sub>, K<sub>RRCenc</sub>, K<sub>RRCint</sub> (per 5.3.13.3);  
  - Suspend SRB1 and SDT-configured bearers;  
  - For each SDT radio bearer: indicate PDCP suspend and re-establish the RLC entity per TS 38.322;  
- The procedure ends.  
- RRC_INACTIVE UE continues monitoring paging while T302 runs.  
- If T331 is running, idle/inactive measurements continue per Clause 5.7.8.

Upon receiving an RRCRelease message, the UE shall perform the actions specified in **Clause 5.3.8** (as explicitly stated in Clauses [1] and [3]: *“The UE shall: … perform the actions as specified in 5.3.8”* and *“The UE shall: perform the actions as specified in 5.3.8.”*).

Per **Clause 5.3.8.3**, these actions include:

- Delaying subsequent actions by **60 ms** from RRCRelease reception (or earlier, if lower-layer ACK is indicated);  
- Stopping timers **T380**, **T320**, **T316** (if running), **T350**, and **T346g**;  
- Clearing **VarRLF-Report**, if T316 was running;  
- If AS security is **not activated**, ignoring all fields except `waitTime` and transitioning to **RRC_IDLE** with release cause *‘other’* (per 5.3.11);  
- If `redirectedCarrierInfo` indicates E-UTRA redirection: handling `cnType` and/or `voiceFallbackIndication` per TS 23.502;  
- If `cellReselectionPriorities` or `freqPriorityListNRSlicing` is present: storing priority info and applying it (with optional T320 start if `t320` is included);  
- If `deprioritisationReq` is present and supported: starting/restarting **T325**, storing the request;  
- If `measIdleConfig` is present: stopping **T331**, storing idle measurement parameters, and starting **T331** (if `setup`);  
- If `suspendConfig` is present: resetting MAC, applying suspendConfig (except `nextHopChainingCount`), configuring SDT (if `sdt-Config` present), suspending all SRBs/DRBs/MRBs (except SRB0), indicating suspension to upper layers, entering **RRC_INACTIVE**, and performing cell selection — *unless* `waitTime` is present (triggering RRC_IDLE instead);  
- If `waitTime` is present: starting **T302**, applying access barring (for all categories except ‘0’ and ‘2’), stopping **T390**, and performing actions per **5.3.14.4**;  
- Otherwise (i.e., no `suspendConfig` and no valid `waitTime`/redirection/suspend): performing actions upon going to **RRC_IDLE** per **Clause 5.3.11**, with release cause *‘other’*.  

Additionally, the UE shall discard stored inter-RAT cell reselection priority info and apply broadcast system information priorities (per end of Clause [1]).

Per **Clause 5.8.10.2.4**, when the UE receives a command to remove a sidelink measurement object (`sl-MeasObjectId`):

- For each `sl-MeasObjectId` in the received `sl-MeasObjectToRemoveList` that exists in `VarMeasConfigSL`’s `sl-MeasObjectList`:  
  → Remove that entry from `sl-MeasObjectList`;  
  → Remove all associated `sl-MeasId`s from `sl-MeasIdList`;  
  → For each such removed `sl-MeasId`:  
  &nbsp;&nbsp;– Remove its measurement reporting entry from `VarMeasReportListSL` (if present);  
  &nbsp;&nbsp;– Stop the periodic reporting timer and reset associated info (e.g., `sl-TimeToTrigger`).  
- *Note*: The UE does **not** treat the message as erroneous if an `sl-MeasObjectId` in the removal list is not currently configured.

Per **Clause 5.8.10.5.1**, the purpose of the `MeasurementReportSidelink` procedure is:  
→ To **transfer NR sidelink measurement results from the UE to the peer UE** (i.e., for sidelink communication, not to the network).

A UE in RRC_CONNECTED shall use the resource pool indicated by `sl-TxPoolExceptional` for NR sidelink communication transmission under **any** of the following conditions (per clauses 5.8.8 and 5.8.13.3, adapted for communication):

1. **T310 for MCG or T311 is running**, *and* `sl-TxPoolExceptional` is included in `sl-FreqInfoList` for the concerned frequency in SIB12 **or** in `sl-ConfigDedicatedNR` within RRCReconfiguration (Clause 5.8.8, 5.8.13.3);  
   — *Note: In this case, the UE configures sidelink resource allocation mode 2 (random selection) using `sl-TxPoolExceptional`.*

2. **T301 is running**, *and* the cell on which the UE initiated RRC connection re-establishment provides SIB12 including `sl-TxPoolExceptional` for the concerned frequency (Clause 5.8.8, 5.8.13.3);

3. **T304 for MCG is running**, *and* the UE is configured with `sl-TxPoolExceptional` included in `sl-ConfigDedicatedNR` for the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration (Clause 5.8.8, 5.8.13.3);

4. The UE is configured with `sl-UE-SelectedConfig`, *and* a result of sensing on resources in `sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal` (for the concerned frequency) is **not available** in accordance with TS 38.214, *and* `sl-TxPoolExceptional` is included in either:
   - the received RRCReconfiguration (`sl-ConfigDedicatedNR`), **or**  
   - SIB12 (`sl-FreqInfoList`) provided by the PCell (Clause 5.8.8);

5. The UE is **not yet configured with `sl-ConfigDedicatedNR`** (i.e., from RRC connection establishment/resume until receiving RRCReconfiguration, RRCRelease, or RRCReject), *and* SIB12 includes `sl-TxPoolExceptional` for the concerned frequency (Clause 5.8.8);

6. A result of sensing on resources in `sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal` (in SIB12) for the concerned frequency is **not available** in accordance with TS 38.214, *and* SIB12 includes `sl-TxPoolExceptional` for that frequency (Clause 5.8.8).

In all cases above, the UE configures lower layers to perform **sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection** using the pool indicated by `sl-TxPoolExceptional` (TS 38.321).

Per Clause 5.7.15.2 (1) and (2):  
- The UE shall consider the Timing Advance value for SRS for Positioning transmission to be invalid;  
- The UE shall release the `srs-PosRRC-InactiveConfig`.  

Additionally, per Clause 5.3.13.6 (1) &gt; (2):  
- Since cell reselection occurs while T319 is running, the UE shall perform the actions upon going to RRC_IDLE as specified in Clause 5.3.11 with release cause **'RRC Resume failure'**.  

Thus, the UE:  
1. Releases `srs-PosRRC-InactiveConfig`;  
2. Invalidates the associated TA;  
3. Transitions to RRC_IDLE with release cause 'RRC Resume failure'.

Triggers (per Clause 5.7.3.2):  
- Detecting radio link failure for the SCG (Clause 5.3.10.3);  
- Detecting beam failure of the PSCell while the SCG is deactivated (TS 38.321);  
- Reconfiguration with sync failure of the SCG (Clause 5.3.5.8.3);  
- SCG configuration failure (Clause 5.3.5.8.2);  
- Integrity check failure indication from SCG lower layers concerning SRB3.

One specific action upon initiation (per Clause 5.7.3.2):  
- If not initiated due to beam failure of the PSCell while SCG is deactivated, the UE shall **suspend SCG transmission for all SRBs, DRBs, and (if any) BH RLC channels**.

Per Clause 5.5.2.11, if `gapSharingFR1` is set to `setup` and an FR1 measurement gap sharing configuration configured by `gapSharingFR1` is already setup, the UE shall:

1. Release the existing FR1 measurement gap sharing configuration configured by `gapSharingFR1`;  
2. Setup the new FR1 measurement gap sharing configuration indicated by `measGapSharingConfig`, in accordance with the received `gapSharingFR1` as defined in TS 38.133.

Upon receiving an RRCReconfiguration message, the UE shall perform the actions specified in **Clause 5.3.5.3**, which include:

- Processing configuration updates (e.g., SCG activation/deactivation if `scg-State` is present — Clause 5.3.5.3, 1>2>);
- Handling DAPS source release if `daps-SourceRelease` is included (Clause 5.3.5.3, 1>3>);
- Applying other dedicated configurations (e.g., radioBearerConfig, spCellConfig, SCell additions/modifications/releases per Clauses 5.3.5.5.8, 5.3.5.3, etc.).

**If the RRCReconfiguration includes `reconfigurationWithSync`**, the UE **shall execute the “Reconfiguration with sync” procedure** as defined in **Clause 5.3.5.5.2**, which entails:

- If AS security is not activated: perform actions upon going to RRC_IDLE (Clause 5.3.11) with release cause *‘other’* — procedure ends (**5.3.5.5.2, 1>**);
- If no DAPS bearer is configured:
  - Stop T310 and T312 for the corresponding SpCell (if running);
  - For MCG: stop T316 (if running), clear `VarRLF-Report`, resume MCG transmission if suspended;
  - Start T304 for the SpCell using `t304` from `reconfigurationWithSync`;
  - Identify the target SpCell via `frequencyInfoDL`/`physCellId` or fallback to source SSB frequency;
  - Start synchronising to DL of target SpCell;
  - Apply BCCH configuration (Clause 9.1.1.1) and acquire MIB (**5.3.5.5.2, 1> else**);
- If any DAPS bearer is configured:
  - Create MAC entity for target cell group (mirroring source);
  - Establish RLC/logical channels for each DAPS bearer and SRB in target cell group;
  - Suspend SRBs for source cell group;
  - Apply `newUE-Identity` as C-RNTI for target cell group;
  - Configure lower layers per `spCellConfigCommon` and additional fields;
  - Reset MAC entity and deactivate unlisted SCells (**5.3.5.5.2, 2> If any DAPS bearer is configured**);
- If UE is a L2 U2N Remote UE: perform PC5-RRC connection release (**5.3.5.5.2, 2> if UE is connected with L2 U2N Relay UE**).

Note: This procedure is triggered immediately upon reception (per NOTE 1 in 5.3.5.5.2), and applies regardless of whether the RRCReconfiguration is received over SRB1 or SRB3 (though SRB3 delivery invokes DLInformationTransferMRDC handling per Clause 5.7.1a.3, which then dispatches to 5.3.5.3 → 5.3.5.5.2).
